# Component reductions B.5.9–10

`conclusion_of_source` constructs a minimal best offender, a normal moved
component, all five literal B.5.9 action alternatives and the B.5.10 product
and module configuration. The natural branch uses the proved equality
U=[C_V(O₂(LA)),L]=[V,L], retaining possible central summands in C_V(O₂(LA)).
`Conclusion.descent` supplies the actual complementary-factor B.5.11 consumer.

The parent's B.5.8 centralization and three-rank-one reductions remain explicit,
as do the four universal earlier implications B.5.1, B.5.5, B.4.8(2) and A.2.1.
`Assembly` records their exact interfaces and source owners. No B.5.9–10 result,
chief-factor bound or model-dependent product premise remains assumed.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined 1 March 2004 manuscript, printed pp.106–109.
-/
